Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Early Career Software Engineer* role at *Flow Engineering*. At Sperse, I have shipped AI-powered features across the stack: a Python, LangGraph, LangChain, and FastAPI multi-agent platform that routes requests through 40+ specialized agents for 10,000+ users, paired with a TypeScript/Node.js and React Flow interface for authoring and managing durable agentic workflows. That experience maps directly to Flow's need for engineers who can own complete features and bring AI into the center of how technical teams reason about complex systems.

I have also built the infrastructure that makes agentic systems reliable in production. I developed evaluation harnesses and prompt and model management workflows using OpenTelemetry trace-based evals in GitHub Actions CI/CD, catching latency, accuracy, and safety regressions before release. I created a FastMCP server that exposes 160+ validated backend actions to AI agents with secure access controls, monitoring, and live Redis progress tracking. Earlier at Qualitest, I designed distributed systems and APIs with Java, Spring Boot, PostgreSQL, and Redis, and orchestrated long-running AWS workflows across more than 100,000 weekly executions. Together, these projects have trained me to build pragmatic backend services, data pipelines, observability, and full-stack product experiences while communicating technical decisions clearly.

Flow's mission to help humanity design products faster, simpler, and safer is compelling because the impact reaches rockets, satellites, aircraft, and other systems where engineering rigor matters. I am especially drawn to Flow's values of moving with urgency and shipping a V1 before iterating: my agentic code-review workflow automated triage across 25–30 pull requests each week, while my customer-facing workflow work taught me to observe real usage and improve the system quickly. I would bring that same bias toward execution, curiosity about requirements engineering for hardware, and willingness to learn from experienced engineers and customers.

I would welcome the opportunity to help Flow build assisted requirement drafting, consistency checks, impact analysis, and intelligent suggestions for systems and domain engineers. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

